10","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
{"parentUuid":"9a66e048-a4a2-4a2f-86e5-183de5f96687","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"22f73e5a-b0a5-47e4-9913-8f18c2e92429","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YNoTasNDQ8jD9oppL94Ujm","type":"tool_result","content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 6 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: shadow-diagnostic-method\n3\tdescription: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses, annotated images of board parts)\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-25T16:53:44.069Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n12\t\n13\tWhenever a message mentions a board component, connector, fuse or test point, also send an annotated image showing where it is (user asked on 2026-10-25). Use the user's own photo when it covers the spot; otherwise annotate the manual's layout (page 2-9) rotated 90° clockwise, which matches how the board is mounted in the backbox (J130 at the bottom, J101 on the right, fuses F101–F105 vertical with F101 left and F105 right). A pre-rotated copy is in `docs/manuel-the-shadow/2-9_PD_implantation_orientee-comme-montee.png`. Draw with PIL, save in `photos/`, send with SendUserFile.\n14\t\n15\tBefore asking for a series of measurements, say in one or two sentences what it protects against (the goal is never to reconnect a repaired Power Driver into a fault), and keep the series minimal: skip values already measured, try the most likely point first. The user questioned a 16-reading table (\"À quoi ? Est-ce que ça me sert ?\").\n16\t\n17\t**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them.\n18\t\n19\t**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's fuse table swaps F104 and F105 (the Power Driver schematic is right: F104 → J107-2 Red-Brown, F105 → J107-3 Red-Black) and its solenoid table has errors (Sol 08 is on Red-Black), so map coil supplies by measurement.\n20\t"}]},"uuid":"f9b0a3d4-1bd5-4ada-9411-b16ce8ecc11f","timestamp":"2026-11-01T12:48:27.460Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md","content":"---\nname: shadow-diagnostic-method\ndescription: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses, annotated images of board parts)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n  modified: 2026-10-25T16:53:44.069Z\n---\n\nFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n\nWhenever a message mentions a board component, connector, fuse or test point, also send an annotated image showing where it is (user asked on 2026-10-25). Use the user's own photo when it covers the spot; otherwise annotate the manual's layout (page 2-9) rotated 90° clockwise, which matches how the board is mounted in the backbox (J130 at the bottom, J101 on the right, fuses F101–F105 vertical with F101 left and F105 right). A pre-rotated copy is in `docs/manuel-the-shadow/2-9_PD_implantation_orientee-comme-montee.png`. Draw with PIL, save in `photos/`, send with SendUserFile.\n\nBefore asking for a series of measurements, say in one or two sentences what it protects against (the goal is never to reconnect a repaired Power Driver into a fault), and keep the series minimal: skip values already measured, try the most likely point first. The user questioned a 16-reading table (\"À quoi ? Est-ce que ça me sert ?\").\n\n**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times. Finding parts from designators alone was hard for them.\n\n**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` and `photos/` folders next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic, user photos); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step). The manual's fuse table swaps F104 and F105 (the Power Driver schematic is right: F104 → J107-2 Red-Brown, F105 → J107-3 Red-Black) and its solenoid table has errors (Sol 08 is on Red-Black), so map coil supplies by measurement.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9a66e048-a4a2-4a2f-86e5-183de5f96687","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
